WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:07.180
The FBI has served a search warrant on Republican
Senator Richard Burr for his stock trades

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.400
around the Corona virus pandemic.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:14.299
You might remember that Richard Burr was one
of the senators exposed to making very convenient

00:00:14.299 --> 00:00:18.270
stock trades right after being briefed about
the coming pandemic.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.280
But before that, knowledge was public.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.660
An investigation is under way.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:27.130
Federal agents have now seized any number
of elements from Richard Burr, including his

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.130
cell phone.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:32.820
Recall that Richard Burr is the senator who
sold a bunch of stock on February 13th.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:36.879
This was when the Senate Intelligence Committee
was already regularly being briefed about

00:00:36.879 --> 00:00:38.520
the coming pandemic.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.269
Trump publicly was downplaying it and Republicans
publicly were downplaying it as well.

00:00:43.269 --> 00:00:48.480
And a whole bunch of those shares of stock
lost massive amounts of value in the weeks

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.890
that followed as the effect of coronavirus
hit the markets.

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:57.219
And Richard Burr was able to avoid significant
financial losses by these trades.

00:00:57.219 --> 00:00:59.949
Now, do I think that this investigation is
serious?

00:00:59.949 --> 00:01:04.680
Because, after all, we're talking about Donald
Trump's attorney general, William Barr's Justice

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:05.680
Department.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:09.420
This is one of the most politically biased
justice departments that we've seen in a long

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.420
time.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:15.390
Do I really believe that they are going to
go hard against Republican senators?

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:19.980
I hate to say it, but my instinct is that
this is basically a show.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:24.579
And I'll tell you what, what the counter counter-factual
would be in a moment.

00:01:24.579 --> 00:01:25.579
So.

00:01:25.579 --> 00:01:26.579
Okay.

00:01:26.579 --> 00:01:27.579
Yeah.

00:01:27.579 --> 00:01:28.579
They got to get a warrant.

00:01:28.579 --> 00:01:29.579
You have to have.

00:01:29.579 --> 00:01:31.539
Already done a bunch of work to convince a
judge that there's probable cause that Richard

00:01:31.539 --> 00:01:32.700
Burr committed a crime.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:33.700
I get it.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:34.700
Yes.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:37.799
To serve a search warrant to a sitting U.S.
senator, it means it was approved in the Justice

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:39.690
Department at the highest levels.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:43.659
But I have a very difficult time believing
that this is going to go very far.

00:01:43.659 --> 00:01:49.340
Now, one thing I will mention is that if this
gets to more senators than maybe it is serious

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:51.799
because Richard Burr was not the only one.

00:01:51.799 --> 00:01:57.310
We had Republican Senator Kelly Loffler from
Georgia dumped huge amounts of stock.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:00.670
But shares of Citrix, which makes telework
software.

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:05.969
One thing I want to remind you of, because
it's relevant here is insider trade trading

00:02:05.969 --> 00:02:08.100
versus the STOCK Act.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:13.220
There's some confusion between insider trading
from an S.E.C. perspective and violations

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:14.620
of the STOCK Act.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:18.909
When we talk about insider trading in general,
you're typically trading a company's stock

00:02:18.909 --> 00:02:23.950
because of nonpublic information usually about
that company.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.280
It's not always illegal.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:29.250
It depends on when you make the trade, what
the information is, a whole bunch of other

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.250
factors.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.290
And it's governed by the Securities and Exchange
Commission.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:38.480
The S.E.C., the STOCK Act is a specific piece
of legislation that applies to members of

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:42.910
Congress and it applies to the trading activities
of members of Congress specifically.

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:47.519
This was needed because members of Congress
could trade on inside information that was

00:02:47.519 --> 00:02:51.950
not about a particular company, but it was
more related to nonpublic briefings.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:56.760
Intelligence related to it could be national
security, foreign policy or whatever else.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:04.220
It would potentially not be illegal per the
yesI sees insider trading laws in some cases

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:07.360
something that would be trading that violates
the Stock Act.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:08.840
Important to understand.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.299
So the Stock Act was meant to deal with that.

00:03:11.299 --> 00:03:12.959
It was passed in 2012.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:15.220
It was then weakened in 2013.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:16.890
Now this is really interesting.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:23.500
The Stock Act passed in the Senate 96 to three,
ninety six to three of the three people to

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:24.980
vote against it.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:30.810
One happens to be Richard Burr, the exact
Republican senator that we're talking about

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:31.810
today.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:32.900
Now, let me mention one other thing.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:34.480
This is very cynical.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:39.640
There were many Republican senators involved
in this apparent insider trading around Corona

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:40.640
virus.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:44.030
So far, it's only Richard Burr who has been
served a warrant.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:49.370
It just so happens that Richard Burr is the
only one of the senators who allegedly did

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:53.020
this insider trading, who signed on to a Senate
report.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:58.540
Because, again, he's part of the Senate Intelligence
Committee, which found Trump Russia collusion.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:00.310
He signed his name to it.

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:06.189
Is Burr being targeted as retribution while
so far Kelly Loffler and the others have not

00:04:06.189 --> 00:04:07.189
been?

00:04:07.189 --> 00:04:08.189
I don't know.

00:04:08.189 --> 00:04:12.260
The Trump Justice Department, which wrongly
summarized Robert Mueller's report as total

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:13.260
exoneration.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:18.120
That was a lie, recently decided they didn't
want to prosecute Michael Flynn, who pleaded

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.120
guilty.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:20.650
They said, yeah, we're not going to prosecute
him.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:23.949
And they've now figured out how to get Paul
Manafort out of prison, which we'll talk about

00:04:23.949 --> 00:04:25.320
on the bonus show.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:30.840
I would not put it past this Justice Department
to target Richard Burr and not the others

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:36.680
because of his signing on to the Trump Russia
report that the Senate Intelligence Committee

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:37.680
put out.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:38.680
That's what we know so far.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:39.680
We will follow it.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:40.680
Let me know what you think.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:05:52.620
I'm on Twitter at 
David Pakman.

